# New Features Plan - astro-content-hub

Status: Phase 1 COMPLETE (committed locally, not yet pushed/deployed)
Last updated: 2025-07-24

This document audits the current feature set, identifies the gaps a typical
content/docs site should close, and proposes a prioritized roadmap. It is a
plan only - nothing here is implemented yet. After the human confirms, we
break it into tasks and execute one by one.

---

## 1. Current state audit

What the hub already does well:

- **Landing page** - hero, latest posts, feature cards, projects grid,
  principles, CTA (`src/pages/index.astro`).
- **Blog** - listing + catch-all article route, nested-dir slugs, draft filter,
  per-post tags/author/source frontmatter.
- **Product docs** - data-driven per product, sidebar nav with `order` sorting,
  breadcrumb, dedicated `index` route.
- **Product landing pages** - dynamic from the `products` array
  (`src/config/products.ts`), no per-product route files.
- **i18n** - `en` (default, no prefix) + `zh` (`/zh/...`), per-page fallback
  (never a 404 on a missing translation), locale switcher, `hreflang`.
- **Mobile UX** - hamburger nav overlay, collapsible docs sidebar.
- **SEO basics** - `<title>`, meta description, Open Graph tags, hreflang.
- **Markdown** - Shiki (`css-variables` theme), relative-`.md`-link rewriting at
  build time, `.prose` shared typography.
- **Deploy** - static output, GitHub Pages + Cloudflare Pages, base-path aware
  (`withBase()`).
- **Content sync** - external repos sync posts/docs via a PR-based GitHub Action.

Confirmed gaps (by inspecting `dist/`):

- Rendered headings have **no `id` attributes** (Sätteri does not auto-slug),
  so TOC and anchor links are currently impossible.
- **No `<link rel="canonical">`** on any page.
- **No `og:image`** on the landing page (and no default social image).
- **No** custom 404 page.
- **No** `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, or RSS/Atom feed.
- **No dark mode** (light-only; `--color-bg-dark` exists but only as a fixed
  dark surface for footer/accents, not a switchable theme).
- **No** table of contents, heading anchor links, copy-code button, prev/next
  nav, tag pages, search, reading time, or JSON-LD.

### Architectural constraints (shape every feature below)

1. **Static output, no UI framework.** Client-side behavior is vanilla `<script>`
   tags, not React/Vue. Keep it that way.
2. **Single global stylesheet** (`src/styles/global.css`) on CSS custom
   properties. New theming (e.g. dark mode) extends the token system, not ad-hoc
   colors.
3. **Minimal deps.** `package.json` currently has only `astro` + `@astrojs/check`
   + `typescript`. Adding a dependency requires explicit human authorization
   (AGENTS.md). Several features below are designed to need **zero** new deps.
4. **i18n route mirror.** Every new page route needs a `src/pages/zh/` twin
   (the documented pattern). This is a real per-feature cost: a new route = 2
   files. (404 is the exception - one locale-aware page.)
5. **Build must stay green.** `npm run build` runs `astro check` (strict, 0
   errors/warnings expected) then builds. Every feature must keep it green.

---

## 2. Gap catalog

Organized by category. Each item is tagged with **Importance** (I), **Cost** (C,
T-shirt size), **New dep?**, and the **i18n route tax** (does it add a zh/
mirror?).

### A. SEO & discoverability

| # | Feature | I | C | New dep? | zh mirror? | Notes |
|---|---------|---|---|----------|------------|-------|
| A1 | `robots.txt` | High | XS | No | No | Static file in `public/`. Points to sitemap. |
| A2 | Canonical URLs | High | XS | No | No | One `<link rel="canonical">` in `Layout.astro`. |
| A3 | `sitemap.xml` | High | S | Optional | No | `@astrojs/sitemap` (1 dep, robust, base-aware) OR a custom `src/pages/sitemap.xml.ts` endpoint (0 dep). |
| A4 | RSS feed | High | S | Optional | No | `@astrojs/rss` (1 dep) OR custom `rss.xml.ts` (0 dep). Posts already have date/description. |
| A5 | Default OG image | Medium | S | No | No | A static `public/images/og-default.png` + `og:image` default in `Layout.astro`. |
| A6 | JSON-LD structured data | Medium | S | No | No | `Article` schema on posts, `BreadcrumbList` on docs. |

### B. Reading & content UX

| # | Feature | I | C | New dep? | zh mirror? | Notes |
|---|---------|---|---|----------|------------|-------|
| B1 | Dark mode / theme toggle | High | M | No | No | Dark token block + toggle in Nav + no-FOUC inline script. Highest UX impact. |
| B2 | Heading anchor IDs | High | S | No | No | Small mdast slug plugin (same pattern as `remark-rewrite-links.mjs`). Unlocks B3/B4. |
| B3 | Table of contents (docs) | High | M | No | No | Right-rail TOC from Astro `render().headings` in `DocsLayout`. Needs B2. |
| B4 | Heading anchor links | Medium | S | No | No | `#` link beside each heading. Needs B2. |
| B5 | Copy-code button | High | S | No | No | Small client script on `<pre>` blocks. |
| B6 | Prev/next nav (docs) | Medium | M | No | No | Uses existing `order`; compute prev/next from the sidebar list. |
| B7 | Reading time | Low | S | No | No | Word-count at build time; show on post header + PostCard. |
| B8 | Reading progress bar | Low | S | No | No | Cosmetic; thin top bar on article pages. |

### C. Content discovery & navigation

| # | Feature | I | C | New dep? | zh mirror? | Notes |
|---|---------|---|---|----------|------------|-------|
| C1 | Custom 404 page | High | S | No | No (1 page, locale-aware) | `src/pages/404.astro`, links home/posts. |
| C2 | Tag pages `/posts/tags/[tag]` | Medium | M | No | Yes (×2) | Posts have `tags`; no browseable tag index yet. |
| C3 | Related posts | Medium | M | No | No | By shared tags on the article page. |
| C4 | Client-side search | High | L | Yes (Pagefind) | No | Pagefind runs as a post-build step; indexes all pages. Heaviest item. |
| C5 | Breadcrumbs on posts | Low | S | No | No | Docs already have them; mirror on articles. |

### D. Markdown / authoring

| # | Feature | I | C | New dep? | zh mirror? | Notes |
|---|---------|---|---|----------|------------|-------|
| D1 | Admonitions/callouts | Medium | M | No | No | `> [!note]` GitHub-style via a custom mdast plugin. |
| D2 | Image optimization | Low | M | No | No | `astro:assets` `<Image>`; affects content authoring. Lower priority (sample content). |

### E. Site / ops

| # | Feature | I | C | New dep? | zh mirror? | Notes |
|---|---------|---|---|----------|------------|-------|
| E1 | Analytics (Plausible/Umami) | Situational | XS | No | No | One script tag in `Layout`. Only if tracking is wanted. |
| E2 | `/about` page | Low | S | No | Yes (×2) | Content page; needs copy. |

---

## 3. Prioritized roadmap (recommended)

Phased so each phase delivers standalone value, keeps the build green, and
minimizes new dependencies. Phases 1-2 are the highest-leverage work and need
**zero** new deps.

### Phase 1 - SEO & site essentials (zero deps, ~1 session)

Goal: make the site discoverable and never show a bare 404.

1. **A1 robots.txt** - `public/robots.txt` pointing to the sitemap (once A3
   lands; safe to add the line now).
2. **A2 Canonical URLs** - add `<link rel="canonical" href={abs(currentPath)}>`
   in `Layout.astro`. ~3 lines.
3. **C1 Custom 404** - `src/pages/404.astro`, locale-aware (detect from path),
   links to home + posts + docs. One file, no zh mirror needed.
4. **A3 Sitemap** - **recommend `@astrojs/sitemap`** (robust, base-aware,
   respects the `site` config). Adds 1 dep. Fallback: custom `sitemap.xml.ts`.
5. **A4 RSS feed** - **recommend `@astrojs/rss`** for `/rss.xml` (posts, latest
   20, locale-aware: `/rss.xml` for en, `/zh/rss.xml` for zh). Adds 1 dep.
   Fallback: custom endpoint.

**Deliverable:** site is crawlable, has a feed, never 404s bare, every page is
canonical.

### Phase 2 - Reading UX (zero deps, ~1-2 sessions)

Goal: bring docs/article reading up to modern expectations.

6. **B1 Dark mode** - dark color tokens under `:root[data-theme="dark"]`, a
   toggle button in `Nav`, and an inline `<script>` in `<head>` (runs before
   paint) reading `localStorage` + `prefers-color-scheme` to prevent FOUC.
   Highest single-feature UX impact.
7. **B2 Heading anchor IDs** - a small mdast visitor plugin (same shape as
   `remark-rewrite-links.mjs`) that slugs `h1`-`h4` `id` attributes. Unlocks
   B3/B4.
8. **B3 Table of contents** - `DocsLayout` gets a right-rail `<nav>` built from
   `render().headings` (already returned by Astro, just not consumed). Active
   section highlight via IntersectionObserver (small client script). Responsive:
   collapses on mobile.
9. **B5 Copy-code button** - a client script that wraps `<pre>` blocks with a
   "Copy" button using `navigator.clipboard`. Scoped to `.prose`.
10. **B6 Prev/next (docs)** - compute prev/next from the ordered sidebar list in
    `renderLocalizedPage`; render at the bottom of `DocsLayout`.

**Deliverable:** dark mode, navigable docs with TOC + prev/next, copyable code.

### Phase 3 - Content discovery (zero deps, ~1 session)

Goal: help readers find more content.

11. **C2 Tag pages** - `/posts/tags/[tag]` + `/zh/posts/tags/[tag]`. Aggregate
    tags across all published posts (incl. fallback), list PostCards. Add a
    "Tags" link to the posts page header.
12. **C3 Related posts** - on the article page, show 2-3 posts sharing the most
    tags. Compute in `posts/[...slug].astro`.
13. **B4 Heading anchor links** - `#` link beside each heading (now possible
    after B2).
14. **C5 Breadcrumbs on posts** - mirror the docs breadcrumb pattern.

**Deliverable:** tag browsing, related posts, anchor links.

### Phase 4 - Polish & advanced (selective)

Pick what's worth the cost; these are lower ROI.

15. **D1 Admonitions** - GitHub-style `> [!note]` / `[!warning]` callouts via a
    custom mdast plugin. Nice for docs, medium effort.
16. **A5/A6 OG image + JSON-LD** - static default OG image; `Article` JSON-LD
    on posts.
17. **B7 Reading time** - word count at build time.
18. **C4 Search (Pagefind)** - the highest-cost item. Only if the site grows
    large enough to need it. Pagefind runs as a post-build step
    (`pagefind --site dist`) and ships a small client bundle. Adds a build tool.
19. **E1 Analytics** - only if tracking is wanted; one script tag.
20. **E2 About page** - content page, needs copy.

---

## 4. Recommendation summary

**Do Phases 1-3.** They deliver the features a typical content/docs site is
expected to have, cost **zero new dependencies** (except Phase 1's sitemap +
RSS, where I recommend the official integrations for robustness - 2 small
deps), and each phase is independently shippable.

**Within Phase 1, do A1/A2/C1 first** (robots, canonical, 404) - they are
trivially small, high value, and need no deps at all. Sitemap + RSS can land
in the same PR or a follow-up once the deps are authorized.

**Phase 2 dark mode is the single highest-impact UX feature** - do it early.
It touches `global.css` (new dark token block) and `Nav`/`Layout` (toggle +
no-FOUC script) but no routes, so the i18n tax is zero.

**Defer Phase 4** except admonitions (D1) if docs authors want callouts. Search
(C4) is the only genuinely expensive item; add it only when the site has enough
content to justify it.

### Dependency asks to flag up front

Phase 1 recommends two new dev dependencies (both official Astro integrations,
low risk):

- `@astrojs/sitemap` - generates `sitemap-index.xml` from the build, base-aware.
- `@astrojs/rss` - generates the feed from posts.

Both are opt-in: each has a zero-dep custom-endpoint fallback if the human
prefers to avoid the deps. **Decision needed:** integrations vs. custom
endpoints.

### i18n note (not a feature, an observation)

The `src/pages/zh/` route mirror is the documented pattern, but it doubles
every new route file. Phases 1-3 add ~4 new routes (404 is exempt, tag pages
are the only route-bearing feature), so the cost is ~6 extra files - manageable.
If route count grows further, a future refactor to a `[locale]`-segment approach
could eliminate the duplication, but that is a separate, higher-risk change and
is **not** recommended now.

